# {{ project_name }}

{% if project_type == 'python-api' -%}
A small Python API project foundation.
{% elif project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' -%}
A small Python API and Streamlit UI project foundation.
{% else -%}
A small, language-neutral project foundation.
{% endif %}

## Development

Use [Mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/) to install the tools and run the project's development tasks.

{% if project_type == 'python-api' -%}
Run the API with `uv run {{ project_name }}`. It serves `/health` on port {{ api_port }}.
{% elif project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' -%}
Run the API with `uv run {{ project_name }}` and the UI with `uv run streamlit run {% if separate_packages %}services/ui/src/{{ project_name | replace('-', '_') }}_ui{% else %}src/{{ project_name | replace('-', '_') }}{% endif %}/ui.py --server.address 0.0.0.0 --server.port {{ ui_port }}`.
{% endif %}

{% if include_containers %}
## Containers

Build the API image with `docker build -f Dockerfile.api -t {{ project_name }}-api:local .`.
{% if project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' %}
Build the UI image with `docker build -f Dockerfile.ui -t {{ project_name }}-ui:local .`.
{% endif %}
{% if include_compose %}
Run the local services with `docker compose up --build`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if include_kubernetes %}
## Kubernetes

Review the rendered resources with `kubectl kustomize kubernetes/base`. Build and
make the referenced images available to your chosen cluster before applying
these manifests. The template does not create or configure a cluster.
{% endif %}
{% if include_flux %}
## Flux

The `kubernetes/flux` bundle requires an existing Flux controller and
reconciliation root to include these files. It does not install Flux or apply
resources.
{% endif %}

{% if project_type != 'generic' %}
## Quality and selected modules

Initialize Git, run `mise install --locked` and `mise run setup`, and commit the resolved `uv.lock`.
Run `mise run lint`, `mise run format-check` and `mise run test`.
{% if include_coverage %}
Tests enforce {{ coverage_threshold }}% coverage and produce XML/HTML reports. UI launch code is excluded; add browser tests for UI interactions.
{% endif %}
{% if include_pre_commit %}
Setup installs lint/format and commit-msg hooks once this directory is a Git repository.
{% endif %}
{% if include_persistence %}
SQLite uses `DATABASE_PATH` (default `data/app.sqlite3`); `/items` and `/items/{key}` are a key/value starter. Compose data and Kubernetes PVCs are generated when those modules are selected. Review backups and storage before production.
{% endif %}
{% if include_security_scanning %}
CI enforces dependency/code/secret and selected container scans. Vulnerabilities fail the workflow; configure narrow reviewed exceptions where appropriate.
{% endif %}
{% if include_release_automation %}
Configure `RELEASE_TOKEN` for Release Please; review and merge release PRs to publish tags.
{% endif %}
{% if include_image_publishing %}
Release tags publish images to `ghcr.io/{{ image_registry_namespace }}/{{ project_name }}-api`{% if project_type == 'python-api-with-ui' %} and `{{ project_name }}-ui`{% endif %}. Configure GHCR permissions before tagging.
{% endif %}
{% if include_gitops_promotion %}
Review/copy `gitops/` contents into `{{ gitops_repository }}`, configure `GITOPS_TOKEN`, and add the Flux objects through your existing reconciliation root. Dev changes push to GitOps `main`; production changes require a PR merge.
{% endif %}
{% if include_k3d %}
Install Docker, kubectl and k3d 5.9.0. Use `mise run k8s-setup-local`, `k8s-sync-local`, `k8s-status`, `k8s-logs`, and `e2e-test`. Teardown requires `python scripts/cluster.py down --yes` and deletes cluster data. E2E creates and removes only its unique disposable cluster.
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
Full module documentation: https://github.com/merlrwx/devops-template/blob/v1.1.0/docs/features.md
